Two directories are pictures rather than code, and the licence covers them the
same way. What follows is not a second licence, it is a note about what they
are, because a reader who finds them will wonder.

  docs/art/    one plate per version, painted once by tools/chronicle-art.sh
               through Cloudflare Workers AI and committed as an ordinary file.
               Machine-made from a prompt built out of the commit; nobody sat
               and drew one. A plate can be repainted.

  docs/faces/  one portrait per pilot, painted the same way and never again.
               A face is somebody's, in the sense that matters here rather than
               the sense a court would use: the manifest is the lock, no flag
               exists to overwrite one, and adding a flag is a rule change. If
               a pilot wants their face out of the book, that is their call and
               it needs no argument.

The rest of the media in media/ is hand-made and covered by the licence above.
